<!--
  ZA.Saga v4.0.0 - intentional API breaks for the major version bump, #173.

  ZeroAlloc.Outbox 3.0 replaced FetchPendingAsync with a lease-based claim, so that concurrent hosts
  never dispatch the same message twice. Saga 4.0 moves onto it:

  - ZeroAlloc.Saga.Outbox no longer runs a poller of its own. OutboxSagaCommandPoller and
    OutboxSagaPollerOptions are removed (CP0001). WithOutbox() registers one IOutboxTypeDispatcher
    per saga command type, and ZeroAlloc.Outbox's OutboxWorkerService dispatches saga commands.
    Options move to OutboxOptions, set through AddOutbox().
  - ZeroAlloc.Saga.Outbox.Redis's RedisOutboxStore implements the Outbox 3.0 IOutboxStore. The
    Outbox 2.x FetchPendingAsync and the three lease-less marks are removed (CP0002); ClaimPendingAsync,
    RenewLeaseAsync, ReleaseLeasesAsync and the lease-taking marks are their replacements.

  Generated by apicompat in suppression-file mode against the 3.1.1 baseline, then annotated. Only
  the members involved in this change are listed, so an accidental removal elsewhere still fails
  the job. See docs/migrating-to-v4.md.
-->
<Suppressions>
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0001</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>T:ZeroAlloc.Saga.Outbox.OutboxSagaCommandPoller</Target>
    <Left>lib/net10.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.Outbox.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net10.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.Outbox.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
    <Justification>#173: removed. It fetched, dispatched and marked without a lease, so two hosts dispatched the same saga command, and next to AddOutbox it raced Outbox's worker on one table. OutboxWorkerService now dispatches saga commands.</Justification>
  </Suppression>
